    "name": "ChessTutor - AI-Powered Chess Learning Platform",
    "description": "Developed a research-backed full-stack web application that combines the Stockfish chess engine with Large Language Models to help beginners understand *why* strong chess moves work instead of simply recommending them.\n\n**Technologies:** React, TypeScript, JavaScript, OpenAI API, Stockfish, chess.js, react-chessboard\n\n**Highlights**\n\n* Built an interactive chess sandbox with undo/redo, side switching, adjustable AI difficulty, and \"what-if\" analysis tools.\n* Integrated the Stockfish engine to evaluate positions and generate the top candidate moves from any board state.\n* Engineered prompts that transform engine evaluations into beginner-friendly explanations of strategy, tactics, king safety, and positional play using the OpenAI API.\n* Implemented a conversational AI tutor that maintains board-state context, allowing users to ask follow-up questions about specific positions and chess concepts.\n* Designed the application to bridge the gap between optimal engine moves and human understanding, creating a personalized learning experience for new chess players.\n",
